# Fluid networks

Pressurised pipe networks described once as a `Net`, compiled by `network` into an immutable `Network`, and solved for steady heads and flows, simulated through time with tanks, demand patterns and controls, and used to carry a constituent, the age of the water, or heat. Pipes, pumps and control valves share one coupled solver, and every array may carry leading scenario axes and be differentiated.

## Choosing A Surface

| Task | Branch |
|---|---|
| Describe a network and compile it | [Network model](fluid/model.md) |
| Heads and flows at one instant | [Steady hydraulics](fluid/steady.md) |
| Tanks, patterns and controls | [Operation over time](fluid/operation.md) |
| Constituents, water age and temperature | [Transport of quality and heat](fluid/transport.md) |

## Practical Examples

The examples describe the smallest network, solve a network with two loops and run a tank through a day of demand.

